/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 115 0 R
/T (A Demultiplexer \(DEMUX\) is a basic combinational logic element that takes a single input signal and routes it to one of several outputs based on Selector inputs. The selected output is in a HIGH \(1\) state if the input is HIGH, while all other non-selected outputs remain in a LOW \(0\) state.)
/E (A Demultiplexer \(DEMUX\) is a basic combinational logic element that takes a single input signal and routes it to one of several outputs based on Selector inputs. The selected output is in a HIGH \(1\) state if the input is HIGH, while all other non-selected outputs remain in a LOW \(0\) state.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
